      "title": "Upscale Model",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "upscale_model - optional, but pick a CLEAN one, not a SHARP one\n\nThe enlargement is not the finished picture - it is the reference and the frozen context each tile is built on. So halos and invented texture get locked in and copied. Softness costs nothing; putting detail back is this node's whole job.\n\nGood: 4xRealWebPhoto_v4_dat2, 4xNomosUniDAT_otf, RealESRGAN_x4plus,\nrealesr-general-x4v3.\n\nAvoid anything built to look sharp on its own - 4x-UltraSharp, Remacri, NMKD-Siax, and anything with \"Sharp\" in the name.\n\nUse a model whose native scale is equal to or above scale_factor. A 4x model at scale_factor 2.0 is supersampling and looks very good.\n\nFull details: docs/nodes/Y7Nodes_Flux2KleinUpscaler.md"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "upscale_model - optional, but pick a CLEAN one, not a SHARP one\n\nThe enlargement is not the finished picture - it is the reference and the frozen context each tile is built on. So halos and invented texture get locked in and copied. Softness costs nothing; putting detail back is this node's whole job.\n\nGood: 4xRealWebPhoto_v4_dat2, 4xNomosUniDAT_otf, RealESRGAN_x4plus,\nrealesr-general-x4v3.\n\nAvoid anything built to look sharp on its own - 4x-UltraSharp, Remacri, NMKD-Siax, and anything with \"Sharp\" in the name.\n\nUse a model whose native scale is equal to or above scale_factor. A 4x model at scale_factor 2.0 is supersampling and looks very good.\n\nFull details: docs/nodes/Y7Nodes_Flux2KleinUpscaler.md"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -1180,
