      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "The two settings that matter most\n\ntile_size - roughly how big each tile is, and what decides memory use. DOWN if you run out of memory. UP if tiles invent detail that does not\nbelong. \n\noverlap - how far each tile sees past its own edges, so things crossing a seam stay joined up. Costs memory and time. 128 suits most pictures.\n\nA visible seam means tiles drifting in tone, not the blend: raise `overlap`, lower `refine_strength`, or set `color_match`.\n\nToo sharp / too much invented detail? Check in this order:\n  1. the upscale model (see the note by its loader - most common cause)\n  2. refine_strength - try 0.92, then 0.88\n  3. tile_size - bigger tiles invent less fine detail\n\nFull details: docs/nodes/Y7Nodes_Flux2KleinUpscaler.md"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "The two settings that matter most\n\ntile_size - roughly how big each tile is, and what decides memory use. DOWN if you run out of memory. UP if tiles invent detail that does not\nbelong. \n\noverlap - how far each tile sees past its own edges, so things crossing a seam stay joined up. Costs memory and time. 128 suits most pictures.\n\nA visible seam means tiles drifting in tone, not the blend: raise `overlap`, lower `refine_strength`, or set `color_match`.\n\nToo sharp / too much invented detail? Check in this order:\n  1. the upscale model (see the note by its loader - most common cause)\n  2. refine_strength - try 0.92, then 0.88\n  3. tile_size - bigger tiles invent less fine detail\n\nFull details: docs/nodes/Y7Nodes_Flux2KleinUpscaler.md"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
